nodes.prompt:
Brand: {{brand.brand_name}}
What it does: {{brand.brand_summary}}
Voice: {{brand.voice_tone}}
Audience: {{brand.target_personas}}

Hook: {{inputs.hook}}
Beats: {{inputs.beats}}
CTA: {{inputs.cta}}
Casting note: {{inputs.presenter}}

Cast ONE person from the target audience and write a 3-beat selfie video: beat 1 delivers the hook, beat 2 the proof, beat 3 the CTA.

`actor` must pin identity down hard enough that it can be repeated: apparent age, build, hair (colour, length, how it sits), face details worth seeing at arm's length, exact clothing including colour and fabric, and the specific room with named objects in it.

`master_frame_prompt` is a still-image prompt for the neutral opening frame. Structure it: selfie-angle medium close-up of a [age]-year-old [description] with [features], [expression], in [named room with specific clutter]. Describe only the person, wardrobe, room and light — no camera brand names, no quality adjectives, no text.

For each of the 3 shots write:
- `frame_prompt`: an EDIT instruction applied to the master frame, not a new scene. Always start with "Same person, same hair, same clothes, same room." then change only expression, head angle and framing for this beat. Beat 1 should lean slightly toward the camera with raised eyebrows; beat 3 should be warmer and more relaxed.
- `motion_prompt`: what happens in the 8 seconds AFTER that frame — the action and delivery only, since the model already sees the person. Include the spoken line in double quotes.
- `line`: just the spoken words, at most 18 words so it fits in 8 seconds.

`on_screen_text`: one caption per beat, at most 5 words each, for viewers watching muted.
